.TH SPEECH 3
.SH NAME
speech \- the emulator's own speech engine
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B bind -a #W /mnt/speechengine
.sp 0.3v
.B #W/ctl
.B #W/audio
.B #W/text
.B #W/tts
.B #W/voices
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The device is an engine of
.IR speech (4):
it serves the files that interface asks of one, so
.I speech9p
can use it
.RB ( "speech9p -E '#W'" ,
or its ctl's
.BR "engine #W" )
on a machine with no host program to hear or speak for it, a phone
among them.
.TP
.B ctl
.BR start ,
.B end
and
.B cancel
bracket an utterance;
.BI "voice " v
(one of
.BR voices ),
.BI "lang " l
and
.BI "model " m\fR.
A read gives
.BR "name native" ,
.B "rate 16000"
(the rate of
.BR tts 's
sound),
.B stt
and
.BR tts ,
each the engine built in
.RB ( whisper ,
.BR flite )
or
.BR none ,
the model and whether it is loaded, the voice, the language, and how
many utterances and finals there have been.
.TP
.B audio
The utterance's sound, written between
.B start
and
.BR end :
16 kHz, mono, 16-bit little-endian; a minute of it at most.
.TP
.B text
Records, a line each, to every reader from its open on:
.BI "final confidence=" n " " words
when an utterance's end has been recognised, or
.BI "error " reason\fR.
There are no partials.
.TP
.B tts
Write text, at most 4096 bytes; then read its sound on the same open
file to end of file: 16 kHz, mono, 16-bit little-endian.
The reads follow on from the write, whatever their offset.
.TP
.B voices
The voices built in, a line each.
.PP
Recognition is whisper.cpp's, on the utterance once it has ended, in a
process of its own, so
.B end
returns at once and its final comes when it is done.
A model is a file of
.B /lib/speech/models
named by
.BR model ,
loaded at the first utterance after it is set
.RB ( ggml-base.en.bin
unless set).
None is in the tree:
.B tools/speech-models.sh
fetches them, each checked against a SHA-256 it pins.
A model is a name of letters, digits,
.BR . ,
.B -
and
.B _
only, so whoever holds
.B ctl
cannot have the device read anything else.
.PP
Synthesis is flite's, with its voices
.B slt
(the default),
.BR rms ,
.B awb
and
.BR kal16 .
.PP
Each half is built in only where its library is when the emulator is
built (whisper.cpp's pkg-config file; flite's headers).
Without one,
.B ctl
says
.B none
for it; an utterance's end gives
.BR "error no recogniser built in" ,
and a write of
.B tts
is refused.
The boot profile makes the device
.IR speech (4)'s
engine when it can hear; a phone's boot makes it the engine whenever
it has either half.
.SH SOURCE
.B /emu/port/devspeech.c
.br
.B /tools/speech-models.sh
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR audio (3),
.IR speech (4),
.IR dictate (1)
.SH BUGS
Recognition gives finals only, after the utterance, not words as they
are said.
.br
One utterance is recognised at a time; an end while one is being
recognised gives
.BR "error the recogniser is busy" .
.br
The phone builds do not yet build whisper.cpp or flite in.
